                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_219">Fountains, Yorkshire. Cistercian
                        abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>The fragments constituting
                        Additional MS 62132B are identifiable as the pastedowns from <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_2885">Additional MS
                           62132A</ref>. The latter has a Fountains Abbey
                     inscription.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">These missal fragments were with VR 6107 (now
                        <ref target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_2882">Additional MS
                        62129</ref>) when <persName role="fmo">Henry Vyner's</persName> collection
                     of Fountains Abbey books was on loan to the Archives Department of Leeds Public
                     Libraries. Most of these books were subsequently acquired by the British Museum
                     in 1981. Compare the entry for <ref
                        target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_2885">Additional MS
                        62132A</ref>.</provenance>
               </history>
